      "id": "note-1",
      "title": "Graph Algorithms & Shortest Path Cheatsheet",
      "content": "# Graph Algorithms Cheatsheet\n\nEssential algorithms for competitive coding rounds:\n\n## 1. Breadth-First Search (BFS)\n- **Time Complexity**: `O(V + E)`\n- **Space Complexity**: `O(V)`\n- **Use Case**: Shortest path in unweighted graphs.\n\n## 2. Dijkstra's Algorithm\n- **Time Complexity**: `O((V + E) log V)` using priority queue.\n- **Constraint**: Non-negative edge weights.\n\n> Note: For negative weights, use Bellman-Ford `O(VE)`.",
      "folder": "DSA",
      "tags": "graphs, dsa, algorithms, cheatsheet",
      "pinned": true,
      "createdAt": "2026-09-04T10:00:00.000Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-09-05T12:00:00.000Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-2",
      "title": "System Design: Distributed Cache & Eviction",
      "content": "# Scaling Distributed Caches\n\nArchitecture principles for caching layers:\n\n## Eviction Policies\n1. **LRU**: Least Recently Used\n2. **LFU**: Least Frequently Used\n\n## Write Strategies\n- **Cache-Aside**: Application checks cache first; falls back to DB.\n- **Write-Through**: Updates written to cache and DB atomically.",
      "folder": "System Design",
      "tags": "caching, system-design, redis",
